## What the program does (read from the code)

- Metropolis, checkerboard (two sublattice) updates, random initial lattice for every (T, seed) run,
  `--burn` discarded sweeps, then one measurement per sweep.
- Per run it reports means of |m|, m², m⁴, e, e² (per site), chi = L²(<m²> − <|m|>²)/T (the
  "connected" susceptibility built from |m|), c = L²(<e²> − <e>²)/T² and U = 1 − <m⁴>/(3<m²>²).
- `--series DIR` stores per-sweep |m| and e as `L{L}-T{T:.4f}-s{seed}-{m,e}.npy`.
- Measured cost on this host (single process): about 0.27, 0.40, 0.97 and 3.2 ms per sweep for
  L = 32, 64, 128, 256. Stage 1 ≈ 6 CPU-min, stage 2 ≈ 17 CPU-min, stage 3 ≈ 6.5 CPU-min.

## Conventions and reference values to compare against (sourced, not measured here)

- Exact T_c = 2/ln(1+√2) = 2.269185… (Onsager 1944; Kramers–Wannier 1941).
- Exponents: ν = 1, γ = 7/4, α = 0 (log divergence of c). The finite-size susceptibility peak lies
  above T_c, shifted by ∝ L^(−1/ν); for L = 64 a peak near T ≈ 2.3 is expected, so the stage-2 window
  (peak ± 0.12) should contain T_c.
- Binder cumulant at criticality for periodic square lattices: U* ≈ 0.6107 (Kamieniarz & Blöte 1993,
  J. Phys. A 26, 201; U* = 1 − Q/3 with Q ≈ 0.856). Crossings of finite pairs approach T_c with
  corrections ∝ L^(−1/ν−ω).
- Metropolis dynamic exponent z ≈ 2.17 (Nightingale & Blöte 1996): tau_int of |m| at T_c grows
  roughly as L^2.17, so sweep counts that suffice at L = 32 may not at L = 128 or 256. Integrated
  autocorrelation time estimated with Sokal's automatic window (window W ≥ c·tau, c ≈ 5); error bars
  of means use N_eff = N/(2 tau_int).
- Starting from a random lattice at low T, Metropolis may freeze into striped (domain-wall) states on
  a periodic lattice; this can depress |m| and distort chi at the lowest pilot temperatures.

## Analysis choices (plan, see `assignment.json` for who delivers what)

- Stage 1: chi(T) and c(T) per seed and seed-mean; peak = grid argmax of the seed-mean chi, refined
  by a parabola through the points around the maximum; the stage-2 centre is the refined peak rounded
  to 0.01 (stated with the grid argmax for comparison).
- Stage 2 (revised after seeing the data): U(T) per size from seed-pooled moments. Primary T_c: joint
  finite-size-scaling fit U_L(T) = f((T − T_c) L^(1/ν)), ν = 1, f cubic, T = 2.22–2.31, weighted by
  block-bootstrap errors; supporting: model-free pairwise crossings by linear interpolation; robustness:
  fit window/order and free ν. The first plan (one polynomial per size over all 9 points) was rejected:
  U(T) is sigmoidal over the window and all sizes merge at 2/3 below T ≈ 2.22, so low-order polynomials
  cross spuriously there (≈ 2.22). 95% percentile bootstrap resampling seeds with replacement at each
  (L, T), plus a time-series block bootstrap. tau_int of |m| per (L, T, seed) with N/tau_int reported.
- Stage 3: U_256(T) at the 5 temperatures with errors (seeds and block bootstrap of per-run series,
  kept as working data); test whether U_256 passes through the stage-2 crossing point (T*, U*) within
  errors, and report tau_int / equilibration at L = 256 for 10000 sweeps.

## What could not be established in advance

- Whether 2000 burn-in sweeps from a random start equilibrate L = 128 and especially L = 256 near
  T_c (expected relaxation times are of order 10³–10⁴ sweeps there); stage 2's tau_int and stage 3
  will tell.
- With only 3 seeds per point, a seed-level bootstrap has few distinct resamples per point; its
  interval is reported as asked and compared with the time-series block bootstrap.

## Findings that change the plan (recorded as they arise)

- Stage 2: the first-pass crossing estimator was rejected (see the analysis choices above). 20000 sweeps are enough for
  L = 32, marginal for L = 64 and not enough for L = 128 (tau_int(|m|) up to 619 sweeps).
- Stage 3 as specified (L = 256, 2000 + 10000 sweeps from a random start) does not equilibrate: |m| is still
  rising through the runs. Its disagreement with the stage-2 crossing is a sampling artefact, so the check is
  inconclusive. A supplement beyond the design (`data/stage3_long/`, 50000 + 50000 sweeps, same temperatures
  and seeds) is reported separately and does not replace stage 3.
